Open product work

- Report parser and analysis allocation failures reliably. Summary, text
  scope/source and xref data provenance can silently omit facts; index,
  consumer and coverage collectors can fail without explaining why.
- Preserve earlier linker outputs when publishing a later output fails.
  The linker stages all files but publishes them independently; the assembler
  already rolls back its requested output set on detected failures.
- Bound rich-analysis expansion of shared aliases. It currently turns shared
  graphs into trees and can consume exponential memory. Text listings avoid
  this path; focus optimization on demonstrated workloads.
